				(size 0.5 0.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4b932581-4449-4321-b681-706e0f58c7fe")
	)
	(text "240mV - 400 mV\nwhen NRST is pulled down"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 244.602 101.854 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.5 0.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5333cd5f-276f-4751-a27b-28f86f764542")
	)
	(text "maybe this can\nact as a fuse?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.49 104.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5e73908c-64f4-4b8c-9ea3-e092b8f606a4")
	)
	(text "why? you can change this\nin the lab as per performance.\nalso, according to voltage\ndivision, this is a good\nstarting point"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.322 115.57 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "61e749db-8330-47d7-8f54-ab775bc9f6ed")
	)
	(text "why 5k1?\nbecause we're already\nusing 5k1 for USB CCx\npins, and this is to\nmake a better BOM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.754 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "67b19f62-b9b7-4fb0-a459-86349e695f6e")
	)
	(text "this is placed to prevent leakage\ncurrent from turning the transistor on\nspontaneously. similar to MOSFETs I guess....\nBut I think I need to make it a bit smaller,\nnot very small though, or the NPN wont turn on.\nMaking it smaller in LTSpice (2N2222) to around 500\nohms made it unable to achieve saturation. and the\nresistor will also conduct too much current.\nso, if not carefully, this is a double loss."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 36.83 137.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ace8992e-5efa-4608-aa5a-432603763518")
	)
	(text "subject to change\nbased on circuit performance.\nhas to be << 5k1 (other R)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 167.894 102.362 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.5 0.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "bc1492f8-115d-4641-bc3b-3c9a86257ed2")
	)
